d":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximalCliques()":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalcliques()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Every maximal clique once, lazily, each in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order; see ","type":"text"},{"code":"MaximalCliques","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored, and an isolated vertex is a clique of one.","type":"text"}],"title":"maximalCliques()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximalCliques","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"Cliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"title":"Graph","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","abstract":[],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"role":"symbol","title":"MaximalCliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}]}}}